.\" robodr-ros2-watch(1). Source of truth: USAGE in
.\" crates/robodr-ros2-pipeline/src/watch.rs. Keep the two in sync.
.TH ROBODR\-ROS2\-WATCH 1 "2026-10-16" "RoboDR 0.1.0-alpha.1" "RoboDR Manual"
.SH NAME
robodr\-ros2\-watch \- run the RoboDR ROS 2 detection pipeline over captured RTPS traffic
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B robodr\-ros2\-watch
.B \-\-profile
.I profile.json
.B \-\-pcap
.I file
[\fIoptions\fR]
.PP
.B robodr\-ros2\-watch
.B \-\-profile
.I profile.json
.B \-\-interface
.I name
.RB [ \-\-interface
.IR name ]...
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B robodr\-ros2\-watch
runs the RoboDR ROS 2 detection pipeline over captured RTPS traffic and prints
each finding as one JSON line on stdout. It is read\-only: it never sends on the
robot bus.
.SH INPUT
Exactly one kind:
.TP
.BI \-\-pcap " file"
Replay a pcap or pcapng file.
.TP
.BI \-\-interface " name"
Live capture on an interface (Linux, needs CAP_NET_RAW); repeatable;
.B any
= every interface.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-profile " file"
Model profile (JSON). An invalid profile is reported and the run is
observe\-only (never enforcing).
.TP
.BI \-\-domain " id"
ROS_DOMAIN_ID whose well\-known ports are captured (repeatable, 0..=232;
default 0). RTPS on other ports is still caught by the
.B RTPS
magic.
.TP
.BI \-\-dedup " n"
Dedup capacity (default 4096).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-anomalies
Do not report RTPS parse anomalies.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-fragmentation
Do not report fragmented discovery (rejected fragments are always reported).
.TP
.BI \-\-discovery\-server " ip"
Trust announcements relayed from this IP (repeatable).
.TP
.BI \-\-participant\-ip " prefix" = ip
Pin a GUID prefix (24 hex digits) to a source IP (repeatable; several IPs per
prefix allowed).
.TP
.BI \-\-hold\-ms " ms"
How long SEDP from a participant without SPDP is held before it is reported
(default 30000; replays report what is still held at the end).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-binding
Disable the participant/source\-IP binding check.
.TP
.BI \-\-duration " secs"
Live only: stop after this many seconds (then
.B \-\-stats
is printed); default: run until killed.
.TP
.B \-\-stats
Print final counters as JSON on stderr.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
This help.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Done.
.TP
.B 1
Runtime error.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
robodr\-ros2\-watch \-\-profile /etc/robodr/profile.json \-\-pcap lab.pcapng \-\-stats
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR robodr\-commission (1),
.BR robodr\-pulsard (8)
